flybrain relay

A Cloudflare Worker with one Durable Object. The rig (roam.py) POSTs its
latest state and frame here every half second; the public page polls the
Worker once a second and the edge cache answers almost all of it. The rig's
own machine is never reached by a viewer.

Routes

  POST /publish     Authorization: Bearer <PUBLISH_TOKEN>, multipart form with
                    fields state (json text) and frame (jpeg, optional).
                    Body limit 600 KB. Returns {ok:true, seq}.
  GET  /state       the state json plus seq, updated, age, live (age < 15 s)
  GET  /frame.jpg   the latest jpeg, 404 until one has arrived
  GET  /            "flybrain relay <seq>"

Deploy

  cd site/relay
  npx wrangler login
  npx wrangler secret put PUBLISH_TOKEN
  npx wrangler deploy

Then set on the rig, in .env or the environment:

  FLY_RELAY_URL=https://<worker>.workers.dev   (or the custom domain)
  FLY_RELAY_TOKEN=<the same PUBLISH_TOKEN>

and set RELAY in site/web/index.html to the same origin.

The two secrets are PUBLISH_TOKEN on the Worker and FLY_RELAY_TOKEN on the
rig; they must be equal. Nothing else is configured.

Local run

  npx wrangler dev --local --var PUBLISH_TOKEN:devtoken
